  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A new Tripartite Steering Committee was set up for the purpose of the implementation of the Trade for Decent Work Project (T4DW) in January 2021.  The activities carried out within the framework of the T4DW project have revived tripartite dialogue on standards-related activities.  Such activities are expected to also lead to other standard-related results on ratification of ILS and reporting in the next biennium.  The tripartite partners have also been included in several standards-related activities, including through the setting up of the tripartite committee, to review the hazardous work list (the CEACR has been requesting the modification of the list for several years). Through the EU-funded project, which focuses on child labour in the cocoa sector, the Office supported the organization of an online tripartite workshop which took place in April 2021 in the framework of the T4DW project and aimed at addressing issues raised by the CEACR under Convention No. 182 and Convention No. 29 with Government officials, the social partners and participants from other agencies and entities. Furthermore, during this workshop, the ILO provided guidance on how to prepare best for the discussion of the case relating to the application of Convention No. 182 by Ghana, which was discussed by the Committee on the Application of Standards during the International Labour Conference held in June.  This tripartite event also dealt with the information requested by the CEACR to demonstrate the efforts the country is undertaking in the area of child labour and forced labour.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
